menu "Universal Node Gateway profile"

config UN_MEMBERSHIP_LIFECYCLE_HOST
    bool "Advertise Membership Lifecycle Host capability"
    default y
    help
        Advertise the existing V2 Membership Lifecycle Host capability.
        This is a Universal Node capability, not a Gateway-specific role.

config UN_GATEWAY_G1A_ENABLE_PRODUCT_TRAFFIC
    bool "Enable Gateway/OTBR product traffic"
    default n
    help
        G1A keeps the canonical Universal Node foundation isolated.  Enabling
        this starts the existing engineering Gateway HTTP carrier and OTBR
        runtime; that is outside the G1A profile.

config UN_GATEWAY_DEV_P4_AUTH_PREPARE
    bool "Prepare P4 Local authentication runtime (development only)"
    depends on !UN_GATEWAY_G1A_ENABLE_PRODUCT_TRAFFIC
    default n
    help
        Initialize the existing ADR-073 Local authentication transaction table,
        ADR-074 Local session service and P4 access-token association owner
        in G1E mode. This opt-in preparation does not start Wi-Fi, a P4 HTTPS
        listener, Gateway product traffic, or any P4 identity/key provider.
        It must not be enabled in a release configuration.

endmenu
